    {
      "id": "lesson:creative:field-parameters",
      "slug": "field-parameters",
      "title": "Smart Filter Console: field names are not field values",
      "explanation": "A field parameter changes which model columns or explicit measures a visual uses. It is not simply a list of category values. The current Microsoft documentation also describes showing the values of a selected column-based field parameter; this produces hierarchy-slicer behavior and has visual-specific limitations. A console must distinguish choosing the analytical dimension from choosing members of that dimension. Test reset, multiple selection, hierarchy persistence and empty-result states. A parameter does not create missing model relationships or security. Explain the active field in the visual title so a reused chart does not silently change meaning.",
      "objectives": [
        "Distinguish parameter entries from dimension members",
        "Choose a supported console design under model/visual constraints"
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Confirm the report has a local model and define explicit measures where measures will be switched.",
        "Create a Fields parameter through the supported authoring workflow; inspect the generated name/reference/order tuples.",
        "Bind a column parameter to an axis or a measure parameter to values.",
        "Use a separate parameter selector for field names; for column parameters, evaluate the documented Show values of the selected field option in the intended slicer.",
        "Verify selected members and titles after every field change; decide whether and how to clear incompatible prior selections.",
        "Test no selection: the documented parameter behavior is all fields, not an empty-field state.",
        "Use actual underlying fields for drillthrough/tooltip linkage rather than the parameter field itself.",
        "Capture Desktop version and observed behavior before promoting the console."
      ],
      "misconceptions_and_tradeoffs": [
        "A live connection without a local model cannot simply create the parameter.",
        "Measure-based parameters cannot expose category values using the column-value option.",
        "The button slicer has different hierarchy behavior; do not promise identical behavior across slicers."
      ],
      "practice": "A user clears the field selector expecting an empty visual. Redesign the reset instruction without claiming that the parameter supports a none state.",
      "model_feedback": "Explain that clearing means all parameter entries. If the product needs an explicit empty-state workflow, specify and separately validate a report design rather than misdescribing the native parameter.",
      "prerequisite_slugs": [
        "decision-contract",
        "filter-context"
      ],
      "prerequisite_lesson_ids": [
        "lesson:creative:decision-contract",
        "lesson:creative:filter-context"
      ],
      "code_ids": [
        "code:creative:field-parameter"
      ],
