    {
      "id": "lesson:creative:svg-microvisual",
      "slug": "svg-microvisual",
      "title": "Compact SVG indicators: preserve the uncapped number",
      "explanation": "An SVG ring encodes progress in a compact cell; a numeric label carries the actual ratio. The W38 challenge shows inline SVG generated by DAX inside a standard table, under a no-AppSource constraint. This does not mean SVG is always the easiest or fastest choice. Compare a native data bar or a clear actual/target column first. Keep raw progress separate from a visually clamped arc: exceeding a target should remain visible in the number even if a circle cannot show more than one turn. Zero or absent targets need a deliberate unavailable state. The source includes typographic quotation marks in illustrative markup; that text must not be copied blindly as executable XML/DAX.",
      "objectives": [
        "Separate a graphical clamp from a business value",
        "Define accessible alternatives and rendering checks"
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Define Actual, Target, unit, missing-target policy and whether negative actuals are meaningful.",
        "Use DIVIDE for the uncapped ratio; keep blank when a valid denominator is unavailable.",
        "Clamp only the geometric ratio used for the arc, if that is the chosen design.",
        "Construct minimal valid XML with straight quotes and escape data-derived text.",
        "Keep a numeric Actual/Target/ratio column beside the graphic and do not rely on red/green alone.",
        "Check Image URL categorization and support in the target visual/version.",
        "Compare the ring against data bars for reading speed, density and maintenance.",
        "Verify Desktop, service, mobile and export separately; no rendering result is assumed here."
      ],
      "misconceptions_and_tradeoffs": [
        "Clamping the business measure hides overachievement.",
        "A filled arc does not excuse a missing denominator.",
        "A successful browser SVG preview does not prove Power BI rendering or export support."
      ],
      "practice": "A ring shows 100% at both 105% and 180% actual progress. How do you prevent a misleading comparison?",
      "model_feedback": "Keep the raw ratio and actual/target visible. If precise ranking matters, use a bar/table that preserves the magnitude rather than making the ring the only evidence.",
