    {
      "id": "lesson:creative:filter-context",
      "slug": "filter-context",
      "title": "Measures respond to context; stored columns serve a different job",
      "explanation": "A measure is evaluated in the query’s filter context. A stored calculated column expresses row-level values at model-processing time and can support grouping or sorting. Neither choice is universally superior. A reusable report metric must specify the active relationships and filter behavior; adding a slicer cannot repair a disconnected dimension. CALCULATE changes evaluation context according to its filters, so a correct-looking total still needs context tests. Preserve a numeric metric when formatting it: string conversion can undermine numeric sorting, axes and later arithmetic. Dynamic format strings are a relevant alternative when a measure needs different numeric presentation.",
      "objectives": [
        "Choose a measure or grouping column for a stated requirement",
        "Specify filter-context tests for a reusable total"
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Declare fact grain and the intended dimension relationships.",
        "Use an explicit aggregation measure for a filter-responsive total.",
        "Create a column only where a row-level stored value is actually needed for grouping, relationships or another justified task.",
        "Test a single category, multiple categories, date filtering, no matching rows and the grand total.",
        "Check whether totals recompute the business ratio rather than summing or averaging visible ratios.",
        "Use numeric formatting semantics; validate switched units and formats after a field-parameter selection."
      ],
      "misconceptions_and_tradeoffs": [
        "A calculated column cannot reproduce every dynamic slicer-sensitive measure.",
        "CALCULATE is not a generic performance optimization.",
        "A text-formatted number may look correct while losing numeric behavior."
      ],
      "practice": "A currency/percentage switcher uses FORMAT for every result. What should be reviewed?",
      "model_feedback": "Check whether the result must remain numeric for charts and calculations, and assess dynamic format strings. Do not change the underlying arithmetic merely to fix display.",
      "prerequisite_slugs": [],
      "prerequisite_lesson_ids": [],
      "code_ids": [
        "code:creative:safe-variance"
      ],
      "doc_patterns": [
